1
00:01:38,190 --> 00:01:43,900
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,750
[Episode 1]

3
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,710
Being pushed to the brink

4
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:36,280
often happens in an instant.

5
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:40,079
I misstepped

6
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,910
and got trapped in the rubble.

7
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,520
It feels just like last winter.

8
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:49,280
I was

9
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:51,150
caught in a dilemma

10
00:02:53,079 --> 00:02:54,000
I even tried

11
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,030
to figure out

12
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:58,350
when the gears of fate started turning.

13
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,500
Was it that phone call?

14
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,120
No.

15
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:07,400
It must have been that snow.

16
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:11,870
I thought going so far south,

17
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:13,280
I'd be safe.

18
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,710
But I never expected

19
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,470
it would snow there, too.

20
00:03:18,150 --> 00:03:21,270
[One year ago, Shenzhen]

21
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:23,560
Hello.

22
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,180
Can the surgery be postponed?

23
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:27,120
Dr. Liu,

24
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,079
what's going on with you?

25
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:31,140
Are you not satisfied with the price?

26
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:31,960
You know

27
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,470
the surgeons here

28
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:34,150
can't perform this surgery.

29
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,840
If you don't come now,

30
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,910
this patient will die.

31
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,150
What do you mean surgery

32
00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:01,520
inherently carries risks?

33
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,240
I'm telling you.

34
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,800
You killed my daughter!

35
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,910
Give my granddaughter back to me!

36
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,430
Give my granddaughter back to me!

37
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:08,960
I want you to pay
with your money and your life!

38
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,800
The family demanded

39
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,190
750,000 in compensation

40
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,280
from the hospital.

41
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:15,260
[Shenzhen Shenya Hospital]

42
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,310
Since you performed
an unauthorized surgery

43
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:19,149
[“Top 10 Young Physicians”
Award Certificate—Liu Zhengliang]

44
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:17,430
in another location,

45
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:19,000
and it violated hospital regulations,

46
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,279
the insurance company

47
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,610
won't pay a single cent.

48
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,120
We will now announce
the medical association's

49
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,240
findings on whether

50
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:28,650
Beijiang New District General Hospital

51
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,310
committed medical malpractice

52
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:31,710
in its treatment of Li Ya.

53
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,430
For the reputation of the hospital,

54
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:38,510
we have to make this decision.

55
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,070
Stop drinking ice water all the time.

56
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:02,190
It's bad for your stomach.

57
00:05:02,190 --> 00:05:03,920
It's for you. It'll help purify the air.

58
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:04,630
Thanks.

59
00:05:04,750 --> 00:05:05,680
You like playing games.

60
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,510
This is for you.

61
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:08,070
Hope you beat my record in three years.

62
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:08,750
Thanks.

63
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:10,920
You're always leaving
your pens everywhere.

64
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:11,830
Take this pen holder.

65
00:05:11,830 --> 00:05:12,560
It's useful.

66
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:13,950
Just peel off the sticker.

67
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:15,680
Okay, you're too kind.

68
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,750
Stop playing on your phone all the time.

69
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:20,350
Books are man's best friend.

70
00:05:20,430 --> 00:05:21,310
A good book for you.

71
00:05:21,310 --> 00:05:22,040
It's useful.

72
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:23,510
Okay, thanks.

73
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:26,360
Everyone, well,

74
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:28,790
thanks for your hard work

75
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,590
over all these years.

76
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:34,750
He got cocky about his skills

77
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:37,010
and started doing surgeries on the side.

78
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:39,270
This is what happens
when you don't fit in.

79
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:40,720
He only knows skills
but not how to behave.

80
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,920
No one is willing
to stick their neck out for him.

81
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,950
to celebrate his leaving. My treat.

82
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:46,310
Great!

83
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,580
Why did you ask me to come here?

84
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:16,200
I'm out of money.

85
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,620
What's wrong with you?

86
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:23,120
I did a freelance surgery, and it failed.

87
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:23,800
All my money

88
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,390
went to compensate the patient's family.

89
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:26,990
What's that got to do with me?

90
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:28,480
We broke up a year ago.

91
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:29,800
But this car

92
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,120
was bought together

93
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,580
when we were still dating.

94
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,490
What do you mean?

95
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,240
I still have
to be responsible for this car?

96
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:38,830
No.

97
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,560
Well,

98
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:42,830
you were the one

99
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:43,950
who insisted on
buying this car back then.

100
00:06:43,950 --> 00:06:45,190
But now I really need the money,

101
00:06:45,190 --> 00:06:46,120
so I want to sell it.

102
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:46,870
Selling it on

103
00:06:47,630 --> 00:06:48,960
a second-hand platform

104
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:49,870
is too slow.

105
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:51,000
I really can't wait.

106
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,800
I just wanted to know:

107
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,120
if I could give you a big discount,

108
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,070
would you buy it?

109
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:04,150
I don't think you can
sell this car anymore.

110
00:07:04,510 --> 00:07:05,390
Why?

111
00:07:23,430 --> 00:07:25,120
Oh my God.

112
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:28,200
How did you park the car?

113
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:32,040
I have a whole family to feed.

114
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,510
I finally found a job.

115
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:36,560
Do you even know what kind of car this is?

116
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,720
This is a Rolls-Royce.

117
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,480
A Rolls-Royce.

118
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,510
You couldn't afford it
even if you sold me.

119
00:07:40,510 --> 00:07:41,310
Man, man, man.

120
00:07:41,870 --> 00:07:44,800
I'll give you this car as compensation.
Is that okay?

121
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:45,600
Hello,

122
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:48,360
the number you have dialed
cannot be reached at this time.

123
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,800
Please try again later.

124
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:53,159
The number you have dialed
cannot be reached at this time.

125
00:07:53,159 --> 00:07:54,600
Please try again later.

126
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:55,240
Hello,

127
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:58,000
the number you have dialed
cannot be reached at this time.

128
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:58,750
Please...

129
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:40,669
Hello.

130
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,100
Are you at home?

131
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:44,600
Yes.

132
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:47,440
Let Mom answer the phone.

133
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,080
I called her.

134
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,210
But her phone is off.

135
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,840
Hello, can you hear me?

136
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:00,390
Liu Zhengguang,

137
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:01,720
do you have a bad signal?

138
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,510
Liu Zhengguang, can you hear me?

139
00:09:06,510 --> 00:09:07,200
Say something if you can.

140
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,130
Liu Zhengliang.

141
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,480
Mom is missing.

142
00:09:25,870 --> 00:09:27,670
Here is the weather forecast

143
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:29,320
issued by the Fucheng
Meteorological Observatory.

144
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:31,870
A strong cold front from Siberia

145
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:34,240
is expected to bring significant snowfall

146
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,120
to Fucheng
from Friday night into Saturday.

147
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,630
The snowfall will be heavy,

148
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:39,840
with blizzards in some areas.

149
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,390
The minimum temperature will drop

150
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:43,000
to minus 15 degrees Celsius.

151
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,550
The meteorological observatory also issued

152
00:09:44,550 --> 00:09:45,080
a yellow warning for icy roads.

153
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,740
-Please dress warmly
-This is my first time back

154
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:50,480
-and avoid unnecessary trips outdoors.
-in Fucheng in winter in 23 years.

155
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:52,480
Drivers, please control your speed

156
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,030
and keep a safe distance.

157
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:57,720
[Fucheng Funeral Services Street]

158
00:09:58,050 --> 00:10:03,710
[Xiao'an Paper Offerings Shop]

159
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:10,720
[Fucheng Huaide Funeral Center]

160
00:10:10,770 --> 00:10:13,380
[Complete Funeral Services]

161
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:16,760
Oh, my mother.

162
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:31,750
My mother who can't come back.

163
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:39,640
My beloved mother,

164
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:45,150
the dear mother who can't come back.

165
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:48,240
Mom.

166
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,600
That's pretty much how it'll be, bro.

167
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,120
There will be

168
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:54,120
microphones and a band at that time.

169
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:56,390
The atmosphere will be quite sorrowful.

170
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:57,320
That's great.

171
00:10:57,870 --> 00:10:59,130
Give me another piece.

172
00:10:59,790 --> 00:11:01,320
This piece, “Ten Kneels to Repay
a Mother's Love,” from the 1st

173
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,360
-Bro.
-to the 10th kneel, plus the spoken part, is...

174
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:03,960
Bro.

175
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:05,600
That's enough.

176
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,030
How many times has she
acted this out for you?

177
00:11:07,030 --> 00:11:08,960
Are you going to buy this urn or not?

178
00:11:09,030 --> 00:11:10,080
What are you doing?

179
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,010
What do you mean?

180
00:11:11,270 --> 00:11:12,930
I never said I wouldn't buy it.

181
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:14,560
What's with your attitude?

182
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,480
It's not your own mother
who's dead, is it?

183
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,270
What are you saying?

184
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:17,720
What?

185
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,270
What are you saying?

186
00:11:18,270 --> 00:11:18,840
What did I say?

187
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,550
Can't you speak properly?

188
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:20,440
-How am I not speaking properly?
-Can't you speak properly?

189
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,480
-Calm down.
-What's wrong with me asking?

190
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:21,840
No, no.

191
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,870
Am I not allowed to speak here?

192
00:11:22,870 --> 00:11:24,270
Please calm down.
He's in a bad mood lately.

193
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:24,790
Please bear with him.

194
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:25,920
Who's in a good mood?

195
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,870
Who can be in a good mood
coming to a place like this?

196
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:28,600
I understand you.

197
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,630
I completely understand you.

198
00:11:29,630 --> 00:11:30,200
Bro,

199
00:11:30,390 --> 00:11:31,150
how about this?

200
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:31,870
When the time comes,

201
00:11:31,870 --> 00:11:34,440
I'll throw in another half hour for free.

202
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:36,120
You can see I'm being sincere, right?

203
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:36,910
Is that okay?

204
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:37,630
Look,

205
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:39,240
it's only natural for him
to be particular about the music.

206
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,120
He's filial,

207
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:40,870
isn't he?

208
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:42,000
Are you letting people
spend money here or not?

209
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:42,600
Yes.

210
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,510
Don't worry, bro.

211
00:11:43,510 --> 00:11:44,270
Wait for me a moment,

212
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:44,910
okay?

213
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:46,360
God is watching.

214
00:11:46,720 --> 00:11:47,630
-I don't cut corners.
-I'm only doing this for you.

215
00:11:47,630 --> 00:11:48,560
I'm telling you.

216
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:50,150
Come on, Zhengguang.

217
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,850
Hurry up, come here.

218
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:54,880
What were you doing?

219
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,600
Is all the information on them

220
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,630
checked?

221
00:11:59,270 --> 00:11:59,750
It's all correct.

222
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:00,270
You go quickly.

223
00:12:00,270 --> 00:12:01,150
I'll take care of the shop.

224
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:01,390
Okay.

225
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:02,510
And the corn

226
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:04,120
is ready. Do you want one?

227
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,120
I won't eat, sis.

228
00:12:05,750 --> 00:12:06,720
Zip up your jacket.

229
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,780
It's cold outside.

230
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:17,300
[Deyun New Life Technology Center]

231
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:21,550
[Winter Clearance!
Must Go! Grab a Bargain!]

232
00:12:21,650 --> 00:12:27,260
[Missing Person]

233
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,620
♪ I keep my mouth shut,
but inside I'm wound up tight ♪

234
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:27,630
♪ I act like nothing's wrong,
but it hurts again at night ♪

235
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:36,740
[A Tearful Plea for Justice]

236
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:30,730
♪ This town is so big,
yet I dive right in ♪

237
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:33,550
♪ Let them laugh all they want,
I've got to find her ♪

238
00:12:33,930 --> 00:12:36,500
♪ Enough with the "that's enough" crap ♪

239
00:12:37,030 --> 00:12:39,670
♪ You keep running your mouth,
and I'm boiling inside ♪

240
00:12:40,070 --> 00:12:42,460
♪ Say what you want about me.
I'll take it ♪

241
00:12:42,830 --> 00:12:45,220
♪ But drag my mom into this,
and you'll regret it ♪

242
00:12:45,850 --> 00:12:48,230
♪ I'm no tough guy, and I'm no hero ♪

243
00:12:48,590 --> 00:12:50,770
♪ I usually let things slide
and meet you halfway ♪

244
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,000
Usually at this time,

245
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:54,250
♪ But I won't back down this time ♪

246
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,200
she would have finished posting and left.

247
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,630
Why is she still posting them today?

248
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:57,430
♪ I have to bring my mom home.
Everything else can wait ♪

249
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,960
Because she loves doing it.

250
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,750
Don't you have to work overtime
at your job, too?

251
00:12:57,850 --> 00:13:00,190
♪ Grab me by the collar.
I still won't back down ♪

252
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,320
Is that the same?

253
00:13:00,510 --> 00:13:03,210
♪ I've held it all in.
Don't think you can walk away ♪

254
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,480
What your mom is doing

255
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:04,030
is affecting the appearance
of the neighborhood.

256
00:13:03,850 --> 00:13:06,030
♪ Nobody act tough. Nobody start a fight ♪

257
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:04,840
Don't...

258
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,670
don't exaggerate.

259
00:13:05,670 --> 00:13:06,480
What are you doing?

260
00:13:06,370 --> 00:13:09,020
♪ Even if I get nowhere,
I'll still fight you ♪

261
00:13:07,150 --> 00:13:07,960
I mean,

262
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,960
if she works overtime,
I'll work overtime, too.

263
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:10,960
I'll scrape all the posters

264
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,150
off these streets for you.

265
00:13:12,150 --> 00:13:14,360
I'll clear everything,
whether I was supposed to or not.

266
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,670
That way, it won't
interfere with your work.

267
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,000
Just ignore her for now.

268
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:21,440
Okay. It's not easy for you either.

269
00:13:21,540 --> 00:13:23,830
♪ I used to think she nagged me
way too much ♪

270
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:22,960
Thank you, bro.

271
00:13:24,130 --> 00:13:26,720
♪ Now it's quiet without her,
and it just feels wrong ♪

272
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,840
♪ So many things I meant to say,
always thinking there was time ♪

273
00:13:30,090 --> 00:13:32,760
♪ Now when my phone rings,
I'm the first to jump ♪

274
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,750
♪ She'd ask if I was tired.
I'd say, "So what?" ♪

275
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,770
♪ She'd tell me to rest.
I'd sit, then get right back up ♪

276
00:13:39,350 --> 00:13:41,610
♪ I may look upset. So what? ♪

277
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,680
♪ As long as there's no news,
I'll keep pressing you ♪

278
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:45,730
[A Tearful Plea for Justice]

279
00:13:45,010 --> 00:13:47,470
♪ I'm no tough guy, and I'm no hero ♪

280
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,490
[Li Changlu, former head of Fucheng
Paper Mill, is a heartless scumbag.]

281
00:13:46,510 --> 00:13:47,270
[He sold the mill for a song
and pocketed state assets. Shame on him!]

282
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,260
He put over 100 workers out of a job.

283
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,030
♪ I usually let things slide
and meet you halfway ♪

284
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,100
[25 years of fighting for justice,
and still no resolution]

285
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:50,010
[Meanwhile, Li Changlu
fled with the money]

286
00:13:51,050 --> 00:13:53,420
♪ But I won't back down this time ♪

287
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:56,670
♪ I have to bring my mom home.
Everything else can wait ♪

288
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,770
Who told you to clear it?

289
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:05,930
The neighborhood committee.

290
00:14:07,870 --> 00:14:09,080
I don't care who told you to do this.

291
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:11,410
You can't clear it. It's delaying things.

292
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:19,790
Buddy,

293
00:14:19,790 --> 00:14:21,240
can't you understand what I'm saying?

294
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:26,350
[Apartments for Rent]

295
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:22,960
Why don't you look at what I posted?

296
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,840
It's a missing person notice.

297
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:24,910
My mom is missing.

298
00:14:25,150 --> 00:14:25,670
If you take them down,

299
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:27,400
how am I supposed to find my mom?

300
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:28,870
Psycho.

301
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,150
Why are you yelling at me?

302
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:32,210
Your mom is missing. But my mom isn't.

303
00:14:37,030 --> 00:14:38,430
Can you watch your mouth?

304
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,200
Can you watch your mouth?

305
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,200
You want to fight?

306
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,270
Watch your mouth.

307
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,080
What?

308
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:45,910
What?

309
00:14:45,910 --> 00:14:46,390
Let go.

310
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:48,320
You want to fight?

311
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:49,390
Can you talk nicely?

312
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:50,510
Talk nicely.

313
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:52,200
What do you mean, watch my mouth?

314
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,000
What do you mean, watch my mouth?

315
00:14:54,670 --> 00:14:56,000
You wanted to hit me?

316
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,270
Watch your mouth!

317
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,240
My leg. My leg.

318
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:02,970
[Missing Person]

319
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,750
Come on. Exiting passengers go this way.

320
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:08,870
Go inside. Go inside.

321
00:15:08,870 --> 00:15:09,910
Go inside.

322
00:15:10,790 --> 00:15:12,850
Turn left at the intersection ahead.

323
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,620
Come on. Exiting passengers go this way.

324
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,460
Come on. Exiting passengers go this way.

325
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:26,180
Turn left at the intersection ahead.

326
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:29,240
Exiting passengers go this way.

327
00:15:45,030 --> 00:15:46,830
Exiting passengers go this way.

328
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,320
Why are you picking me up?

329
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:49,520
Where's Zhengguang?

330
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,000
He got into a fight

331
00:15:51,670 --> 00:15:52,440
and broke a bone.

332
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,910
It's not a full fracture.
It's a hairline fracture.

333
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:55,440
He's lying in the hospital.

334
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:57,440
Well, well, Liu Zhengguang...

335
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,270
What's in here?

336
00:15:58,270 --> 00:15:59,360
Why is it so heavy?

337
00:15:59,510 --> 00:16:00,080
Books.

338
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:02,960
How childish.

339
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:03,790
Get in.

340
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,800
Now you're home. What do you want to eat?

341
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,150
My mom is missing.

342
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,770
What exactly happened?

343
00:16:18,630 --> 00:16:19,910
I just found out, too.

344
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:25,200
Auntie Ling was diagnosed
with uterine cancer six months ago.

345
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:26,030
When they found out,

346
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:27,540
[Zhanqian Avenue]
[Zhanqian East Station]

347
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:27,690
it had already metastasized.

348
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:31,030
She didn't want to undergo
chemotherapy or radiation therapy.

349
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:33,560
Zhengguang tried
to persuade her many times.

350
00:16:36,630 --> 00:16:38,240
Five days before she left,

351
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:40,750
she left a letter

352
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:41,950
for you two brothers.

353
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,320
We have a lead

354
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,380
that she was asking

355
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,910
about an ice hole before she disappeared.

356
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:48,570
But nothing is confirmed yet.

357
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:58,360
[Stop]

358
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,120
Didn't you usually only stay a few days

359
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,440
when you came
for the Dragon Boat Festival?

360
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,440
Why bring so much luggage this time?

361
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,150
That's all my belongings.

362
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,240
I got fired.

363
00:17:07,839 --> 00:17:08,700
What happened?

364
00:17:15,550 --> 00:17:17,680
I took a freelance surgery job before.

365
00:17:21,069 --> 00:17:22,270
And the patient died.

366
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:26,869
[Stop]

367
00:17:27,109 --> 00:17:28,030
What happened?

368
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:33,750
It snowed that day.

369
00:17:41,750 --> 00:17:43,110
I thought I could do it.

370
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:57,400
[Outpatient]

371
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,680
Apply pressure for three to five minutes.

372
00:17:57,530 --> 00:17:59,780
[Surgery]

373
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:01,780
[Internal Medicine]

374
00:18:03,310 --> 00:18:05,240
We need to contact the fire department
about your mom.

375
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,440
I have a classmate in the fire department.

376
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,970
I'll call and ask him later.

377
00:18:08,510 --> 00:18:09,270
Okay.

378
00:18:09,790 --> 00:18:10,790
That's great.

379
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,070
Thank you, bro.

380
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:15,440
I was too impulsive just now.

381
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:16,550
It's not your fault.

382
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:17,510
No, it's my fault.

383
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:19,110
I've had this problem since I was a kid.

384
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:20,770
I can't help running my mouth.

385
00:18:21,310 --> 00:18:22,160
Me too.

386
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:23,550
What's your name?

387
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:26,160
Jia Xin. The “Xin”
with three "Jin" characters.

388
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:26,720
And you?

389
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:27,720
Liu Zhengguang.

390
00:18:28,030 --> 00:18:29,590
Zheng as in iron-boned.

391
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:30,590
But are your bones made
of glass or something?

392
00:18:30,590 --> 00:18:32,450
One tackle and you got a fracture.

393
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:37,680
Look at my mouth.

394
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:39,160
I just can't control it.

395
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:39,920
It's fine.

396
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,350
You're straightforward.

397
00:18:42,350 --> 00:18:43,920
Bro, you're straightforward.

398
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:44,920
You're a good guy.

399
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,070
What do you do?

400
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:48,960
I don't have a fixed job.

401
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:49,890
I do everything.

402
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,160
My last job

403
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:53,350
was tending the boiler
at a hot spring hotel.

404
00:18:53,350 --> 00:18:54,960
I got the boiler running too hot.

405
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:56,160
And people noticed.

406
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:57,790
Then they reported it.

407
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:58,750
And the place closed down.

408
00:18:58,750 --> 00:19:00,310
People didn't just notice it.

409
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:01,680
They must've felt how hot it was.

410
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,000
Actually, they got burned

411
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,130
while soaking in it.

412
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:07,590
What do you do?

413
00:19:08,070 --> 00:19:09,160
My job...

414
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,060
How should I put it?

415
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,680
I have life-and-death friends
all over the world.

416
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:16,310
Yet I can't find anyone in my own city
to grab a bite or hang out with.

417
00:19:16,310 --> 00:19:17,030
What?

418
00:19:17,750 --> 00:19:18,640
You're working at a crematorium?

419
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,640
Pretty much the same.

420
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:21,110
I sell urns.

421
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:26,110
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

422
00:19:26,110 --> 00:19:27,400
I'll come to you next time I need one.

423
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:27,960
Dr. Chen.

424
00:19:28,030 --> 00:19:29,030
Are you back?

425
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:29,920
I'm back.

426
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,180
Wei is looking for you.

427
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:32,240
They said a patient just came in

428
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,310
with a pistachio stuck in his airway.

429
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:34,440
I'll be right there.

430
00:19:36,510 --> 00:19:37,440
You take my car back.

431
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:38,830
I've already paid the medical bills.

432
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:39,590
You're family.

433
00:19:39,590 --> 00:19:40,750
Talk nicely.

434
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:42,890
Observation bed 5.

435
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:47,140
[Internal Medicine]

436
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,880
I'm eating out.

437
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:51,600
[Don't make noise]

438
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,400
Why didn't you tell me

439
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:03,640
Mom was sick?

440
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:06,480
Mom has terminal uterine cancer.

441
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:07,680
Could you cure her if I told you?

442
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,240
Were you not even

443
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,510
going to tell me

444
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,830
she was missing

445
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:11,590
if I hadn't called back?

446
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:13,030
What's the point of telling you?

447
00:20:13,030 --> 00:20:15,030
How many days a year do you come back?

448
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:29,750
Move over.

449
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:40,040
Have they found Mom's body?

450
00:20:40,830 --> 00:20:41,680
What body?

451
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,000
Who said Mom is dead?

452
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,920
Watch your mouth.

453
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,200
It's obvious

454
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:50,210
that Mom jumped into the ice hole.

455
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,840
The river's frozen over.

456
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,660
We can only wait until spring.

457
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,200
Who said that?

458
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:58,750
Who saw Mom jump into an ice hole?

459
00:20:59,590 --> 00:21:00,510
Did anyone see it?

460
00:21:00,510 --> 00:21:02,510
If no one saw it, she's just missing!

461
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:05,200
Maybe Mom will come back tomorrow!

462
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:05,510
Enough.

463
00:21:05,510 --> 00:21:06,960
Stop yelling, okay?

464
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:12,760
Look at the temperature now.

465
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:14,400
It's hard to find the body

466
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,060
if anyone jumps into an ice hole
in this weather.

467
00:21:17,830 --> 00:21:19,690
Let's try to use our connections.

468
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:22,570
But no matter what,

469
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:25,050
I have to go back to Shenzhen on Friday.

470
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:30,890
Are you even human?

471
00:21:32,350 --> 00:21:33,400
Mom is missing right now,

472
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,960
and you're just going to leave?

473
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:35,480
Look,

474
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,920
the weather forecast said

475
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,790
it will snow in Fucheng on Saturday,

476
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:40,550
so I have to leave on Friday.

477
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,510
The patient is 65 years old.

478
00:21:47,510 --> 00:21:48,270
He was taking care
of his grandson at home.

479
00:21:48,270 --> 00:21:49,160
While eating pistachios,

480
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,270
he found one that wasn't open.

481
00:21:50,270 --> 00:21:51,070
He tried to crack it open with his teeth,

482
00:21:51,070 --> 00:21:52,200
but it went into his airway.

483
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,070
But fortunately, his trachea

484
00:21:53,070 --> 00:21:54,000
is not completely blocked.

485
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:54,910
[Zone C]

486
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,030
He came to the hospital on his own.

487
00:21:55,030 --> 00:21:56,200
How long has the foreign object
been in the airway?

488
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,260
About ten minutes.

489
00:21:57,350 --> 00:21:58,480
No, I still can't get it out.

490
00:21:58,480 --> 00:21:59,720
The shell is too slippery.

491
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,680
Have you tried the Heimlich maneuver?

492
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:01,440
I tried, but it didn't work.

493
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:01,960
Try again.

494
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,310
Okay.

495
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:03,960
Come on.

496
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,080
Slow down.

497
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:19,200
Spit, spit, spit it out!

498
00:22:20,090 --> 00:22:22,380
[Zone E]

499
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:25,320
[Zone E]

500
00:22:33,030 --> 00:22:33,750
No need.

501
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:46,490
It's still not working.

502
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,000
We've tried inserting the bronchoscope

503
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:50,310
several times already.

504
00:22:50,310 --> 00:22:51,640
The trachea is a bit swollen.

505
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:52,310
Get him admitted.

506
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:52,680
Put him under general anesthesia.

507
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:53,920
Use a laryngoscope and a bronchoscope

508
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:55,380
and see if we can remove it.

509
00:23:00,110 --> 00:23:00,750
Wait.

510
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:04,690
It's too slippery to get a grip.

511
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,240
If it really doesn't work,

512
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,970
we'll have to do a tracheotomy.

513
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:13,920
Sit here and wait for me for a while.

514
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:15,250
Hey, what are you doing?

515
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:19,530
Careful.

516
00:23:21,270 --> 00:23:22,200
Hold on, hold on.

517
00:23:22,790 --> 00:23:23,250
Well...

518
00:23:23,350 --> 00:23:24,640
Sir, the pistachio you ate

519
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:25,350
is solid.

520
00:23:25,350 --> 00:23:26,480
Its surface is very smooth.

521
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,550
If we use forceps, it'll just...

522
00:23:27,550 --> 00:23:28,590
Do you have a silicone gel sheeting?

523
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:29,240
Sir, you can't go in there.

524
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,350
I'll go ask and see if I can...

525
00:23:30,350 --> 00:23:32,350
Do you have a silicone gel sheeting?

526
00:23:32,590 --> 00:23:33,070
Wait.

527
00:23:33,790 --> 00:23:34,590
He's a doctor.

528
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:36,680
Do you have any ideas?

529
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:38,920
Do you have
a silicone gel sheeting, surgical sutures

530
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:39,720
and an IV tube?

531
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:40,790
Wait here.

532
00:23:51,750 --> 00:23:53,480
Sir, let's get you some oxygen.

533
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:01,880
The pistachio's surface

534
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:03,000
is covered in mucus,

535
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,350
so it's especially slippery.

536
00:24:04,350 --> 00:24:05,310
If you use forceps

537
00:24:05,310 --> 00:24:06,160
to extract it,

538
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:07,160
it won't be easy.

539
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,350
That's why every time

540
00:24:08,350 --> 00:24:09,550
you reach the glottis,

541
00:24:09,550 --> 00:24:10,680
it slips back down.

542
00:24:11,160 --> 00:24:12,240
It's the same principle as

543
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,000
one of those claw machines.

544
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,460
You can never grab the toy.

545
00:24:15,830 --> 00:24:16,270
In this situation,

546
00:24:16,270 --> 00:24:18,000
you need to think differently.

547
00:24:19,070 --> 00:24:20,070
Make a net

548
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,830
and slide it underneath

549
00:24:23,030 --> 00:24:24,360
to catch the pistachio.

550
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:36,750
Later, give the patient

551
00:24:36,750 --> 00:24:37,810
local anesthesia,

552
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:38,790
and then insert

553
00:24:38,790 --> 00:24:39,550
this net.

554
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,720
Theoretically,

555
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:41,750
it will support the pistachio

556
00:24:41,750 --> 00:24:42,880
from underneath,

557
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:44,160
then you can

558
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:45,550
pull it out like this.

559
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:46,490
Go ahead.

560
00:24:48,310 --> 00:24:48,830
Come on.

561
00:24:50,110 --> 00:24:50,840
Will it work?

562
00:24:51,030 --> 00:24:51,630
Let's try.

563
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,250
We don't have much time.

564
00:24:53,310 --> 00:24:54,840
I'll take responsibility.

565
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:57,440
Open your mouth. Open your mouth.

566
00:24:57,440 --> 00:24:58,370
Open your mouth.

567
00:25:23,550 --> 00:25:24,280
We've got it.

568
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:26,490
Here.

569
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,270
Hang in there.

570
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:31,920
Hang in there, sir.

571
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:34,070
It's out. It's out.

572
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:40,790
It's out.

573
00:25:40,790 --> 00:25:41,440
All right, all right.

574
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:42,000
It's out.

575
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:44,680
You'll be fine.

576
00:25:53,070 --> 00:25:53,930
You'll be fine.

577
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:55,720
It's alright.

578
00:26:18,550 --> 00:26:19,950
What are you laughing at?

579
00:26:20,270 --> 00:26:21,270
I'm not laughing.

580
00:26:21,310 --> 00:26:22,310
Mom's in big trouble now,

581
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:23,680
and you're in the mood to laugh?

582
00:26:23,680 --> 00:26:24,830
You heard wrong. I wasn't laughing.

583
00:26:24,830 --> 00:26:26,290
My nose is uncomfortable.

584
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,200
Your nose is uncomfortable?

585
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:30,400
Why don't you just stop breathing then?

586
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:33,840
Slow down.

587
00:26:34,270 --> 00:26:35,000
Take it slow.

588
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,180
Come on, get in the car.

589
00:26:54,050 --> 00:26:58,660
[Title] [Youyi Road, Jinxiu District,
Fucheng City, Fu'an Province]

590
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,970
[Intersection of Youyi Road
and Ping'an Street]

591
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:23,030
[Beidou Lane-Level Navigation]

592
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:23,920
Turn right.

593
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,160
Turn right.

594
00:27:29,350 --> 00:27:31,310
Don't you know there's traffic
at the intersection?

595
00:27:31,310 --> 00:27:32,480
The GPS told me to go straight.

596
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:33,070
I told you to turn,

597
00:27:33,070 --> 00:27:34,640
so just turn, okay?

598
00:27:34,960 --> 00:27:36,680
What's with that stupid GPS?

599
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:37,880
You've been in Shenzhen for a few years,

600
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:38,720
and you've already forgotten who you are.

601
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,240
right?

602
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:41,270
Do you still remember your name?

603
00:27:41,270 --> 00:27:42,110
Save your scolding for later.

604
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:43,440
I need to take this call.

605
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:48,110
Hello.

606
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:51,310
Hello, is this Dr. Liu?

607
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:52,920
Yes.

608
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:55,240
I went to the hospital for a checkup.

609
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:56,660
What were the results?

610
00:27:56,750 --> 00:27:58,480
The doctor said it's a pituitary tumor.

611
00:27:58,480 --> 00:28:00,410
Fortunately, it was found in time.

612
00:28:00,590 --> 00:28:03,310
I've been admitted to the hospital,
and I'm preparing for surgery.

613
00:28:03,310 --> 00:28:04,680
Thank you so much.

614
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:07,210
I topped up your phone balance.

615
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:09,160
I won't keep you any longer.

616
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:10,070
Thank you. Thank you.

617
00:28:10,070 --> 00:28:10,930
Okay, bye-bye.

618
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:19,040
What are you laughing at now?

619
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:22,520
What's wrong with me laughing?

620
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:24,350
Everything is wrong with it.

621
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:26,440
Our mom's missing,

622
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:28,300
but you don't seem worried at all.

623
00:28:28,750 --> 00:28:29,880
The second someone
mentions going back to Shenzhen,

624
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:31,400
you're ready to fly away.

625
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,530
Do you even have a heart?

626
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:35,680
Were you just hoping

627
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,880
Mom would die sooner,

628
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:37,720
so no one would

629
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:38,880
be a burden to you anymore, right?

630
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:39,920
At the ER,

631
00:28:40,110 --> 00:28:41,240
just because of a few words from me,

632
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:42,440
I saved an old man from the pain

633
00:28:42,440 --> 00:28:44,240
of having his trachea cut open.

634
00:28:44,790 --> 00:28:45,790
And just now,

635
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,070
I learned that a patient

636
00:28:47,070 --> 00:28:47,750
got a second chance at life

637
00:28:47,750 --> 00:28:49,350
because of something I said.

638
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:50,550
What's wrong with being happy about that?

639
00:28:50,550 --> 00:28:51,350
There is something wrong with it.

640
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:52,160
If you cared

641
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:53,110
about Mom even a little bit,

642
00:28:53,110 --> 00:28:54,770
you couldn't possibly laugh.

643
00:28:56,160 --> 00:28:57,720
You've been in Shenzhen for so many years.

644
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:58,960
Whenever Mom talks about you, she cries.

645
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:00,030
Whenever she mentions you, she cries.

646
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:01,230
Has she ever laughed?

647
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:04,310
Maybe I'm not as successful as you,

648
00:29:04,310 --> 00:29:05,310
but I can be there for Mom,

649
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,310
have a few more meals with her,

650
00:29:06,310 --> 00:29:07,200
help her buy groceries,

651
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:08,310
and carry them upstairs for her.

652
00:29:08,310 --> 00:29:09,200
Where are you?

653
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:10,960
I'm a better son than you are.

654
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:22,000
Ah-Guang.

655
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,310
Don't "Ah-Guang" me.

656
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:24,480
Where are you from anyway?

657
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:25,720
What's with the "Ah"?

658
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:27,600
Just call me Liu Zhengguang.

659
00:29:31,590 --> 00:29:32,320
Stop the car.

660
00:29:34,070 --> 00:29:35,200
We're not there yet.

661
00:29:36,070 --> 00:29:37,030
Stop the car.

662
00:29:39,550 --> 00:29:40,160
Stop the car!

663
00:29:40,160 --> 00:29:41,240
Pull over ahead. Pull over!

664
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:42,240
Fine, fine, fine.

665
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:53,750
Liu Zhengguang,

666
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:54,960
you're already in your twenties.

667
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,560
Don't act like a child, okay?

668
00:29:56,590 --> 00:29:57,550
I can't hear you.

669
00:29:57,640 --> 00:29:58,790
Don't tell me what to do.

670
00:29:58,790 --> 00:29:59,720
I don't know you.

671
00:30:07,590 --> 00:30:08,680
Go back by yourself.

672
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:09,540
Leave me alone.

673
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:13,270
I don't have the key.

674
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,050
Now you've got it, okay?

675
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:26,260
I told you to leave, and you actually did?

676
00:30:26,310 --> 00:30:28,110
You won't even spoil me a little?

677
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:57,330
Who are you looking for?

678
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,790
I'm looking for Liu Zhengguang.

679
00:30:59,790 --> 00:31:01,190
I have something for him.

680
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,110
Give it to me.

681
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:03,040
I'm his brother.

682
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:10,030
This is your mother's last letter.

683
00:31:10,790 --> 00:31:12,310
It has been authenticated.

684
00:31:12,310 --> 00:31:14,400
It's indeed in your mother's handwriting.

685
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:15,920
Zhengguang and I are friends.

686
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:18,780
He reported her missing
and brought this letter in.

687
00:31:22,270 --> 00:31:23,720
They still haven't found her.

688
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,920
Don't give up hope.

689
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,700
What's wrong with him?

690
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,760
He didn't even say thank you.

691
00:31:32,030 --> 00:31:33,760
And he came back from a big city?

692
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:12,140
Zhengliang, Zhengguang.

693
00:32:13,750 --> 00:32:16,280
I've been waiting
for this day for a long time.

694
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:20,960
Ever since your father passed away,

695
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:23,480
I've felt that life was meaningless.

696
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:26,200
All these years,

697
00:32:26,270 --> 00:32:27,160
if it weren't for

698
00:32:27,160 --> 00:32:29,240
raising you two little kids,

699
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:32,200
I might have followed him long ago.

700
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:36,310
I knitted a scarf for each of you.

701
00:32:36,830 --> 00:32:39,030
The bankbook is in the big medicine box.

702
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:40,800
Split it between the two of you.

703
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,660
The house goes to Zhengguang.

704
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:44,880
Our place is spacious,

705
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:47,270
but there's a crematorium
across the street,

706
00:32:47,270 --> 00:32:48,670
so it won't sell for much.

707
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:50,450
Zhengguang,

708
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:52,550
you should give
your brother a little extra too,

709
00:32:52,550 --> 00:32:53,590
just as a gesture.

710
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:56,490
Don't fight over
such a small amount of money.

711
00:32:57,480 --> 00:32:59,140
Back then, I bought this place

712
00:32:59,550 --> 00:33:00,960
just so I could watch the smoke

713
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:03,830
rising from the crematorium
when I had nothing else to do.

714
00:33:03,830 --> 00:33:05,200
I always felt I could see

715
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,130
your father's shadow in the smoke.

716
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,880
Others buy houses with ocean views,

717
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:13,610
I bought a house with a view
of the crematorium smoke.

718
00:33:15,550 --> 00:33:16,590
I know you two brothers

719
00:33:16,590 --> 00:33:18,190
each have your own troubles,

720
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:20,610
but who doesn't have problems?

721
00:33:21,350 --> 00:33:22,720
I may be old,

722
00:33:23,510 --> 00:33:24,920
but I'm not experienced.

723
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,730
I don't have any solutions.

724
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,130
You'll have to work it out yourselves.

725
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:32,400
After I'm gone,

726
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:35,240
if you find my body,

727
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,340
just keep the funeral simple.

728
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:40,480
If you can't find it, then forget it.

729
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:42,070
It'll save some money

730
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:44,460
for you two bachelors to get married.

731
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:48,240
If you need me in the future,

732
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:50,960
just burn some paper offerings.

733
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,030
Your father and I

734
00:33:52,350 --> 00:33:54,150
will watch over you from heaven.

735
00:34:27,320 --> 00:34:27,960
Son.

736
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,230
Let me tell you,

737
00:34:29,440 --> 00:34:30,320
today,

738
00:34:30,630 --> 00:34:32,070
you're staying in this room.

739
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,130
You are not allowed to go out, hear me?

740
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:35,510
Also,

741
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:38,540
when you get home, don't tell your mom

742
00:34:38,670 --> 00:34:39,840
that I took you winter swimming,

743
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:40,400
got it?

744
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:43,590
Later,

745
00:34:43,590 --> 00:34:44,880
I'll buy you some candy.

746
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:45,440
Okay.

747
00:34:45,670 --> 00:34:46,280
Liu.

748
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:48,760
Let's split into two teams today

749
00:34:48,760 --> 00:34:49,760
and have a relay race.

750
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:52,150
Let's see who can hold their breath
underwater the longest.

751
00:34:52,150 --> 00:34:53,190
I'm telling you.

752
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:54,449
I'm bored of that game.

753
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:57,280
Then you come up with something.

754
00:34:58,590 --> 00:34:59,450
How about this?

755
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,620
I'll dive from this end

756
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:02,920
all the way

757
00:35:02,920 --> 00:35:03,880
to your side.

758
00:35:04,710 --> 00:35:05,590
If you can swim across,

759
00:35:05,590 --> 00:35:07,360
-I'll cover half of the fine for having
a second child for you. -Be my witness.

760
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:08,560
I'll be your witness.

761
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:22,070
Liu.

762
00:35:22,710 --> 00:35:23,840
Liu!

763
00:36:05,920 --> 00:36:07,230
Liu, swim this way.

764
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,960
Liu! Liu!

765
00:36:10,550 --> 00:36:12,070
Liu!

766
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,710
This way.

767
00:36:35,710 --> 00:36:37,360
Dad!

768
00:37:11,840 --> 00:37:13,500
Ever since the day my dad died,

769
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,590
I became afraid of snow.

770
00:37:16,670 --> 00:37:19,800
Whether it's falling from the sky
or lying on the ground,

771
00:37:20,150 --> 00:37:21,190
as long as I see it,

772
00:37:22,150 --> 00:37:24,210
an overwhelming terror comes over me

773
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:26,760
and pulls me back to that moment.

774
00:37:41,670 --> 00:37:43,330
Is there nothing around here?

775
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:44,070
No.

776
00:37:44,110 --> 00:37:45,630
Let's search farther ahead.

777
00:37:45,630 --> 00:37:47,630
Come on, let's check farther ahead.

778
00:38:01,230 --> 00:38:02,830
Liu, help me take off my gear.

779
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:03,840
Okay.

780
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,110
Thank you. Thank you.

781
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,400
We've been freezing out here all day,

782
00:38:08,400 --> 00:38:09,920
and there's still no sign of her.

783
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,380
Let's call it a day for now.

784
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:12,400
Okay.

785
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:14,190
Thanks, man.

786
00:38:15,190 --> 00:38:17,110
Don't get too anxious.

787
00:38:17,960 --> 00:38:20,110
No news may be good news.

788
00:38:20,630 --> 00:38:21,360
Understand?

789
00:38:21,710 --> 00:38:22,070
Alright,

790
00:38:22,070 --> 00:38:23,270
I'll go let them know.

791
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:40,340
This way. This way.

792
00:38:44,230 --> 00:38:46,070
According to the test results,

793
00:38:46,070 --> 00:38:46,730
the patient

794
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:49,320
has a vascular malformation

795
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:51,000
with associated bleeding as well.

796
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:52,400
This requires surgery

797
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:53,710
to remove it.

798
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:55,360
Is it that serious?

799
00:38:55,360 --> 00:38:56,070
We'll do it.

800
00:38:56,190 --> 00:38:57,320
We'll pay whatever it costs,

801
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:57,840
doctor.

802
00:38:57,840 --> 00:38:59,960
But there's a bit of a problem now.

803
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:00,920
What problem?

804
00:39:00,920 --> 00:39:02,630
Where are my friend's scans?
Can you show me?

805
00:39:02,630 --> 00:39:03,280
The scans are out.

806
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:04,150
Wait a minute.

807
00:39:04,150 --> 00:39:06,150
We're in the middle of a consultation.

808
00:39:06,150 --> 00:39:06,960
Could you step outside first?

809
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:08,220
Go out and wait in line.

810
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:09,070
-Hold on.
-Go ahead, doctor.

811
00:39:09,070 --> 00:39:10,000
Sorry.

812
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:11,400
I'm in a bit of a hurry here.

813
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:11,760
Please wait a moment.

814
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:12,890
Who isn't in a hurry?

815
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:14,920
Can't you see we're talking?

816
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:16,230
You interrupted us halfway through.

817
00:39:16,230 --> 00:39:17,510
The vascular malformation and the problem?

818
00:39:17,510 --> 00:39:18,190
I forgot what you just said

819
00:39:18,190 --> 00:39:18,840
because they...

820
00:39:18,840 --> 00:39:20,000
they interrupted me.

821
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:20,710
Get... get out.

822
00:39:20,710 --> 00:39:21,110
You're just causing trouble.

823
00:39:21,110 --> 00:39:21,480
Don't push me.

824
00:39:21,480 --> 00:39:22,550
-Wait. Wait. -Will you be held
responsible if this gets delayed?

825
00:39:22,550 --> 00:39:23,480
Hey, don't push me.

826
00:39:23,480 --> 00:39:24,480
I'm a doctor here.

827
00:39:24,480 --> 00:39:25,400
I'm a doctor, okay?

828
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:27,510
Even the hospital president
has to wait in line, understand?

829
00:39:27,510 --> 00:39:28,190
Cutting in line?

830
00:39:28,190 --> 00:39:29,070
What are you doing?

831
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:29,800
Keep your hands to yourself.

832
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:30,960
We came from the ER.

833
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:32,230
So did my brother.

834
00:39:32,550 --> 00:39:33,360
Can't you understand or what?

835
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:34,000
Did you rent that mouth or what?

836
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:34,670
Why are you in such a hurry?

837
00:39:34,670 --> 00:39:36,400
-You three are here for the same patient!
-I don't know them.

838
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:40,590
[Authorized Personnel Only;
One Patient, One Visitor]

839
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:37,280
I really don't know them.

840
00:39:37,280 --> 00:39:38,000
We're not here for the same patient.

841
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:38,630
Pull up the scans.

842
00:39:38,630 --> 00:39:39,230
Don't bother arguing with her.

843
00:39:39,230 --> 00:39:39,590
Hurry.

844
00:39:39,590 --> 00:39:40,360
If you squeeze in any farther...

845
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:41,230
-Keep pushing, huh?
-Why are you dragging me?

846
00:39:41,230 --> 00:39:42,070
You still want to squeeze through?

847
00:39:42,070 --> 00:39:42,840
Here.

848
00:39:43,020 --> 00:39:44,630
[Authorized Personnel Only;
One Patient, One Visitor]

849
00:39:43,550 --> 00:39:45,230
Push me again and see what happens.

850
00:39:45,230 --> 00:39:45,760
Hey,

851
00:39:46,230 --> 00:39:47,150
these are my brother's scans.

852
00:39:47,150 --> 00:39:47,800
Step outside first!

853
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:48,550
These are his brother's scans.

854
00:39:48,550 --> 00:39:49,190
My brother's!

855
00:39:49,190 --> 00:39:50,030
His brother's!

856
00:39:50,030 --> 00:39:51,760
My brother's. Don't you get it?

857
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:53,480
You three

858
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:55,150
are here for the same patient!

859
00:39:55,280 --> 00:39:56,400
I... I've been telling you that all along!

860
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:57,150
I said, you three
are here for the same patient!

861
00:39:57,150 --> 00:39:57,840
Why are you

862
00:39:57,840 --> 00:39:58,970
making such a scene?

863
00:40:15,550 --> 00:40:16,550
My name is Ai Chen.

864
00:40:19,510 --> 00:40:20,320
I'm sorry.

865
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:20,800
I didn't know

866
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,400
you were Zhengguang's boss.

867
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:24,710
Why didn't you tell me earlier

868
00:40:24,710 --> 00:40:26,800
that you were Zhengguang's older brother?

869
00:40:26,800 --> 00:40:28,230
I'm not his older brother.

870
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:29,030
He is.

871
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:34,840
How is it?

872
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,920
The vascular malformation is large

873
00:40:38,110 --> 00:40:39,840
and there's associated bleeding.

874
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,100
He needs a craniotomy.

875
00:40:41,960 --> 00:40:42,920
The key is

876
00:40:42,920 --> 00:40:44,550
the location of the lesion.

877
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,030
The lesion is located

878
00:40:46,030 --> 00:40:48,510
adjacent to the posterior part
of the left inferior frontal gyrus,

879
00:40:48,510 --> 00:40:49,840
which is closely related

880
00:40:49,840 --> 00:40:51,370
to the motor speech center.

881
00:40:52,710 --> 00:40:54,880
If anything goes wrong during surgery,

882
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:55,960
the patient could

883
00:40:55,960 --> 00:40:57,420
lose the ability to speak.

884
00:40:57,670 --> 00:40:59,470
This surgery is very difficult.

885
00:41:00,070 --> 00:41:02,190
No one in Fucheng can do it.

886
00:41:03,230 --> 00:41:04,480
You should go to Beijing

887
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:06,630
and find him a hospital
there as soon as possible.

888
00:41:06,630 --> 00:41:08,760
But the patient's current condition

889
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:09,800
is very unstable.

890
00:41:10,110 --> 00:41:11,640
If the bleeding continues,

891
00:41:12,710 --> 00:41:14,440
his life could be in danger.

892
00:41:15,710 --> 00:41:17,840
You family members should

893
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:20,700
quickly discuss your options
and decide what to do.

894
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:22,320
I'll do it.

895
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:24,920
I mean,

896
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,030
are you sure about

897
00:41:26,030 --> 00:41:27,360
this craniotomy thing?

898
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:28,550
If not, let's just go to Beijing,

899
00:41:28,550 --> 00:41:29,110
okay?

900
00:41:29,110 --> 00:41:31,480
Beijing is far away,
and the risk is greater for him.

901
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:32,190
Then what should we do?

902
00:41:32,190 --> 00:41:34,050
You've been working in Shenzhen.

903
00:41:34,360 --> 00:41:35,480
You don't know anyone here.

904
00:41:35,480 --> 00:41:36,360
You said you want to do the surgery,

905
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,150
but how

906
00:41:37,230 --> 00:41:39,030
can you coordinate everything?

907
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:39,920
The biggest problem

908
00:41:39,920 --> 00:41:40,880
is where I'm licensed to do the surgery.

909
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,480
What do you mean by that?

910
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:45,630
It means doctors can only perform surgery

911
00:41:45,630 --> 00:41:48,030
at the hospital where they're registered.

912
00:41:48,190 --> 00:41:49,070
Well, then...

913
00:41:50,320 --> 00:41:51,000
How about

914
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,150
you apply to the hospital

915
00:41:52,150 --> 00:41:54,350
for an out-of-hospital consultation?

916
00:41:54,590 --> 00:41:55,920
That won't work either.

917
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:56,960
He got fired.

918
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:00,760
Fired?

919
00:42:03,110 --> 00:42:05,000
You got fired?

920
00:42:08,070 --> 00:42:11,200
Did they fire you because
you weren't competent enough?

921
00:42:12,800 --> 00:42:14,230
I might not be the best doctor

922
00:42:14,230 --> 00:42:15,150
in the country,

923
00:42:15,150 --> 00:42:16,070
in this specialty,

924
00:42:16,070 --> 00:42:16,760
or in this age group...

925
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:18,090
Then what is your point?

926
00:42:19,510 --> 00:42:20,400
But among my peers,

927
00:42:20,400 --> 00:42:21,600
I'd rank in the top 20.

928
00:42:22,070 --> 00:42:22,710
My goodness.

929
00:42:22,710 --> 00:42:23,800
After everything you said,

930
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:25,360
you only ranked in the top 20?

931
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:26,550
And you're using
your age group as an excuse?

932
00:42:26,550 --> 00:42:27,400
Do you know how many great neurosurgeons

933
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,710
there are in the country?

934
00:42:28,710 --> 00:42:30,070
Why would I need to know that?

935
00:42:30,070 --> 00:42:30,840
Do you know who ranks in the top 20

936
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:31,760
at playing the suona?

937
00:42:31,760 --> 00:42:33,070
-Do you know that?
-Alright, alright.

938
00:42:33,070 --> 00:42:35,150
Don't get off topic.

939
00:42:35,630 --> 00:42:37,760
Zhengguang is lying in a hospital bed.

940
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:38,590
And

941
00:42:38,590 --> 00:42:40,710
a craniotomy is a major operation.

942
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:42,340
You are his older brother.

943
00:42:44,070 --> 00:42:45,400
Can you handle that kind of pressure?

944
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:46,880
Why would I feel pressured?

945
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:48,280
To me, every patient is just a patient.

946
00:42:48,280 --> 00:42:48,760
Besides,

947
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:50,760
Zhengguang and I aren't that close.

948
00:42:51,510 --> 00:42:52,550
Zhengguang said

949
00:42:52,550 --> 00:42:54,410
his brother is cold and arrogant.

950
00:42:55,030 --> 00:42:56,030
Let me tell you,

951
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:57,000
when it really counts,

952
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:57,630
don't mess it up,

953
00:42:57,630 --> 00:42:58,290
you hear me?

954
00:43:01,030 --> 00:43:02,760
Are you really sure about this?

955
00:43:03,840 --> 00:43:05,100
I'm his older brother.

956
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:10,530
I'll take care
of the licensing issue for you.

957
00:43:11,510 --> 00:43:12,190
How?
